.TH GETGROUPS 2 "May 13, 1986"
.UC 5
.SH NAME
getgroups \- get group access list
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <unistd.h>

getgroups(\fIint gidsetlen\fP, \fIgid_t *gidset\fP)
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getgroups
gets the current group access list of the user process
and stores it in the array 
.IR gidset .
The parameter
.I gidsetlen
indicates the number of entries that may be placed in 
.IR gidset.
.B getgroups
returns the actual number of groups returned in
.IR gidset .
No more than NGROUPS, as defined in
.RI < sys/param.h >,
will ever
be returned.
.SH "RETURN VALUE
A successful call returns the number of groups in the group set.
A value of \-1 indicates that an error occurred, and the error
code is stored in the global variable \fIerrno\fP\|.
.SH "ERRORS
The possible errors for \fIgetgroup\fP are:
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
The argument
.I gidsetlen
is smaller than the number of groups in the group set.
.TP
[EFAULT]
The argument \fIgidset\fP specifies
an invalid address.
.SH "SEE ALSO
setgroups(2), initgroups(3)
